<Layout title="Student privacy and communication | Kin & Campus" description="Adult students control their health information. Kin & Campus documents communication preferences and does not collect medical details through this website.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h1>Adult students decide who may receive their health information.</h1><p class="lead">We discuss communication preferences at the beginning of care, document the student's consent, and follow it. A parent may be closely involved, but that involvement must be clear to the student and consistent with privacy law.</p></div>
<div class="w">
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Communication with parents</h3><p>The student chooses what may be shared and with whom. We revisit that preference when circumstances change rather than assuming an earlier answer always applies.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Coordination with other physicians</h3><p>When sharing information with a hometown physician would support safe, continuous care, we use the appropriate authorization and clinical channels.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>This website</h3><p>The introductory form asks only for basic contact and program-fit information. Symptoms, diagnoses, medications, and medical records should never be submitted through it.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="note">If we believe a student faces an immediate threat to health or safety, we will act as permitted or required by law. For an emergency, call 911.</p>
</div>
</Layout>
